# OWL permits punning: one IRI may denote a class AND an individual. The tagged Node
# keeps the populations disjoint BY CONSTRUCTION. If they merge, the class :x
# subseteq bottom would drag the unrelated individual :x into a FALSE inconsistency.
# Expect: coherent; class :x and individual :x independent.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:x a owl:Class .
:x a owl:NamedIndividual .
:C a owl:Class .
:x rdfs:subClassOf :C .
